    {
      "GroupDto": {
        "GroupName": "T0H1N1A6",
        "Description": "NAND reading (inputs A and B, BIAS constantly on, threshold 0.125) of the shipped \u0027Logic Gate NOT-NAND\u0027 gate. Role in the 4-bit adder: first XOR stage of stage 0\u0027s partial sum (chain 6 of 13), Y = NAND(A0, B0), feeding T0H1N26.B. The whole 4-bit adder composes at the logic layer, not optically: every gate\u0027s truth table is extracted once in isolation, so each stage restores clean 0/1 levels by construction \u2014 there is deliberately no multi-stage passive optical cascade here. The fan-out of the A, B and Cin bits onto several gates happens at the logic layer (each gate input is driven by the same network bit); shared stages \u2014 and each stage\u0027s carry-out, which must reach the next stage\u0027s several carry-in pins \u2014 are duplicated as extra gate instances because the canvas wires one waveguide per pin (like NAND1A/NAND1B in \u0027Logic Gate Half Adder\u0027).",
        "Identifier": "group_c103108bb3c3421e8b1d491772d787ed",
        "IdGuid": "154c7b86-59c5-4c00-816e-ee4a2dae09cf",
        "ChildComponentGuids": [
          "27721aeb-03be-4fee-94b0-b38c957ed331",
