    {
      "GroupDto": {
        "GroupName": "T0ORNOT2C5",
        "Description": "NOT reading (input A, BIAS constantly on, threshold 0.375) of the shipped \u0027Logic Gate NOT-NAND\u0027 gate. Role in the 4-bit adder: carry-OR copy 5 of stage 0: Y = NOT(S1 AND C0), feeding T0OROUTC5.B. The whole 4-bit adder composes at the logic layer, not optically: every gate\u0027s truth table is extracted once in isolation, so each stage restores clean 0/1 levels by construction \u2014 there is deliberately no multi-stage passive optical cascade here. The fan-out of the A, B and Cin bits onto several gates happens at the logic layer (each gate input is driven by the same network bit); shared stages \u2014 and each stage\u0027s carry-out, which must reach the next stage\u0027s several carry-in pins \u2014 are duplicated as extra gate instances because the canvas wires one waveguide per pin (like NAND1A/NAND1B in \u0027Logic Gate Half Adder\u0027).",
        "Identifier": "group_3d4567f55aff438191e500e06c4cd32a",
        "IdGuid": "72ce1f90-66fa-4b22-b304-c638febdc59b",
        "ChildComponentGuids": [
          "1a485def-47e2-414e-9219-6ea027fa8fcb",
          "dfa3100d-6645-478c-9c24-5e4831b025de",
          "25efe301-39bb-41d3-a810-7e9721ac533d",
