    {
      "GroupDto": {
        "GroupName": "T0OROUTC10",
        "Description": "NAND reading (inputs A and B, BIAS constantly on, threshold 0.125) of the shipped \u0027Logic Gate NOT-NAND\u0027 gate. Role in the 4-bit adder: carry-out of stage 0, copy 10 of 10: same majority(A0, B0, C0) as T0OROUT, feeding T1H2N5C7.A. The whole 4-bit adder composes at the logic layer, not optically: every gate\u0027s truth table is extracted once in isolation, so each stage restores clean 0/1 levels by construction \u2014 there is deliberately no multi-stage passive optical cascade here. The fan-out of the A, B and Cin bits onto several gates happens at the logic layer (each gate input is driven by the same network bit); shared stages \u2014 and each stage\u0027s carry-out, which must reach the next stage\u0027s several carry-in pins \u2014 are duplicated as extra gate instances because the canvas wires one waveguide per pin (like NAND1A/NAND1B in \u0027Logic Gate Half Adder\u0027).",
        "Identifier": "group_ce39a209b4a4473094e2b94d59edbf1d",
        "IdGuid": "b0ccf732-d235-4025-9f27-d8ed21f0652e",
        "ChildComponentGuids": [
          "fb05e984-67d2-4951-99a7-8054d4b99dae",
          "090b06ef-6199-4be6-9f9d-d63e06265b2d",
