    {
      "GroupDto": {
        "GroupName": "T1H1N5C3",
        "Description": "NAND reading (inputs A and B, BIAS constantly on, threshold 0.125) of the shipped \u0027Logic Gate NOT-NAND\u0027 gate. Role in the 4-bit adder: carry-OR copy 3 of stage 1: Y = NAND(A1, B1), feeding T1H1CARRYC3.A. The whole 4-bit adder composes at the logic layer, not optically: every gate\u0027s truth table is extracted once in isolation, so each stage restores clean 0/1 levels by construction \u2014 there is deliberately no multi-stage passive optical cascade here. The fan-out of the A, B and Cin bits onto several gates happens at the logic layer (each gate input is driven by the same network bit); shared stages \u2014 and each stage\u0027s carry-out, which must reach the next stage\u0027s several carry-in pins \u2014 are duplicated as extra gate instances because the canvas wires one waveguide per pin (like NAND1A/NAND1B in \u0027Logic Gate Half Adder\u0027).",
        "Identifier": "group_aa0447d1374541e9a1c26dbbe09165e9",
        "IdGuid": "6c5e8677-3d8f-4094-89d9-afae9b23bfc6",
        "ChildComponentGuids": [
          "6e342d39-b293-4820-9dfc-ddff21863fe2",
          "792fa47b-dd87-4b9d-9702-554917e0a446",
